14792	{"artifactId":"LLD-613abdb351c2c738-s5","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-613abdb351c2c738-s5-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-14T18:37:11.922Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac1–ac3 and FR001–FR003 of S005 (DEF §6.5) are each designed: the decision joins the repository queue as a 'review-pane' row in the target chat's outbox, survives the panel or window closing, the waiting list is removed, and the start-up sweep keeps a waiting message's attachments.","evidence":"DEF.md:67-69, 174-176 list FR001–FR003 and ac1–ac3. LLD §2.1, §3.2, §5 and §7 design each one: submitExternal goes through ChatQueueWorker.submit with origin 'review-pane', and waitingExternal, drainExternal and dropExternal are removed. The sweep keep set is chatKeep, built from chatStore.list() at extension.ts:476-482. No non-goal is built: there is no daemon queue, no reordering, and nothing is stored in the queue beyond AttachmentRefs. [files: docs/epics/per-repo-chat-turn-queue-outbox-E20261014613abdb3/DEF.md, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"FR004 (attachments of a waiting or failed message are kept until it is finished, cancelled or dismissed) is met, except where the owner's hard 200-session cap rules otherwise.","evidence":"The owner's ruling in commit 895eda8c accepts that a session is evicted at the cap even with live rows. Eviction runs onEvict, which calls chatAttachments.removeSession(id) at extension.ts:469-472, so the attachments of a waiting message in an evicted session are deleted at that moment, not only at the next sweep. The LLD's edge table says the text is kept for a resend, but it does not say the attachments are gone. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/session-file-store.ts]","action":"State in §5's eviction edge case that onEvict deletes the session's attachments, so a resend after eviction carries none.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today submitExternal pushes the message onto an in-memory waitingExternal list. drainExternal runs it directly through runTurn, skipping the queue, and is called at about ten sites. dropExternal discards the list when the panel or host closes.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:204 `const waitingExternal`. Lines 869-879: drainExternal runs `void runTurn(next.text)` and returns early when `worker?.running() === true || queued !== undefined`. Lines 882-889: dropExternal logs 'dropped: the chat panel was closed'. drainExternal is called at 857, 1660, 1666, 1774, 1803, 1828, 1853, 1907, 1928 and 2248. Lines 2243-2250: submitExternal returns 'unavailable', 'queued' or 'sent'. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Failing to save the draft is not detected at submit (trySaveSession only logs). The queue runner reads the store only when the shown session is a different chat, and returns failed 'the chat no longer exists' when the session is missing.","evidence":"turn-lifecycle.ts:122-128: trySaveSession catches the error and calls log.warn. chat-panel.ts:2124-2127: `if (s === undefined || s.id !== message.sessionId) { const found = deps.store.get(...); if (found === undefined) return resolve({ kind: 'failed', error: 'the chat no longer exists' ...`. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"createQueueFactory catches every error from opening the store (a failed mkdir, a node:sqlite load failure, a newer schema, a corrupt file) and returns undefined. Today the chat then stays on a direct path.","evidence":"chat-queue-setup.ts:83-92: a try/catch around createChatQueueStore returns undefined and shows a notice. chat-queue-store.ts:299-304: mkdirSync and openDatabase failures are wrapped as StoreUnavailable('the chat queue could not be opened: …'). Lines 349-356 wrap prepare failures. extension.ts:678 passes the queue only when it is defined. Lines 687-706 and 745 register the command, the context key, the serializer and notifyChat with no condition. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-setup.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused ChatQueueWorker.submit has the stated shape: { sessionId, text, origin: 'typed' | 'review-pane', attachments } → EnqueueResult, where EnqueueResult is ok with the message, or ok:false with reason 'full' | 'busy' | 'unavailable' and a note. It never throws for queue refusals.","evidence":"chat-queue-worker.ts:65-73 declares ChatQueueSubmission and submit(m): EnqueueResult. chat-queue-store.ts:59-61 declares the EnqueueResult union. Lines 408-419: enqueue catches StoreBusy as 'busy' and any other error as a refused result. chat-panel.ts:2178-2181: enqueueTyped already calls trySave and then w.submit with origin 'typed', which is the path the LLD mirrors. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-worker.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The 'review-pane' origin already exists end to end (store column, row mapping, outbox projection), so the outbox (sc5) needs no change.","evidence":"chat-queue-store.ts:44 has `origin: 'typed' | 'review-pane'` and line 266 maps the row's origin. chat-outbox.ts:22 has `readonly origin: 'typed' | 'review-pane'`. No caller passes 'review-pane' today; chat-panel.ts:2180 is the only submit. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-outbox.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The call sites of ExternalSubmitResult, ChatHandOver and notifyChat are chat-panel.ts, docs-review-panel.ts and extension.ts, plus the tests listed in §6. decisionResultLine holds the 'sent', 'queued' and 'unavailable' wording to be changed.","evidence":"Grep finds the following. chat-panel.ts:165 and :181 hold the type. docs-review-panel.ts:45 has `notifyChat?: ((text) => 'sent' | 'queued' | 'unavailable')`, :65 has ChatHandOver, :1603-1611 has handOver (catch → 'failed'), and :2451-2456 has the wording. extension.ts:745 has the only binding. The tests are review-wiring.test.ts:27 (binding regex) and chat-panel.test.ts:4999-5305 (submitExternal suite). One small gap: the `superseding` flag (chat-panel.ts:211, 884, 2230-2236) exists only to keep the waiting list across adopt(), and it becomes dead once dropExternal goes. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"Remove `superseding` along with dropExternal in step 2.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Everything in extension.ts that turns the chat on is in the gating inventory: the insrc.chat.open registration, setContext insrc.chat.ready, the WebviewPanelSerializer and the notifyChat binding. package.json has no commandPalette entry yet.","evidence":"extension.ts:687 calls setContext('insrc.chat.ready', true). Line 688 registers insrc.chat.open, line 697 calls registerWebviewPanelSerializer(CHAT_VIEW_TYPE…), and line 745 binds notifyChat. Grep finds no other use of chatHost. package.json:119-126 has only menus['editor/title'] with when insrc.chat.ready. There is no commandPalette entry. [files: vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts, vscode-plugin/package.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Nothing stored changes. The queue schema, the session files and the attachment directories are untouched, and review-pane rows use the existing origin column.","evidence":"chat-queue-store.ts:373-376: the INSERT already writes the origin column, and :266 reads it back with 'typed' as the fallback. The change only adds new callers of submit and changes internal TypeScript types (ExternalSubmitResult, ChatHandOver). The mixed-version note is accurate: an older plugin's drainExternal (chat-panel.ts:869-879) runs pane messages outside the queue. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"S005 consumes sc1, sc4 and sc5 without redesigning them. It adds no queue reader or writer and leaves the signatures of ChatQueueWorker, the store and the outbox as they are. The changes in chat-queue-setup.ts are limited to the notice text and comments, following the owner's 'chat disabled without sqlite' ruling.","evidence":"The LLD calls only worker.submit (chat-queue-worker.ts:366-379) and drops liveSessionIds consumption. createQueueFactory's signature (chat-queue-setup.ts:83) is unchanged. HLD.md:269 assigns s1 to report 'unsupported VS Code' plainly, and the reworded notices still do that. The disable-the-chat behaviour is the owner ruling recorded in commit 34cb02d0. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-setup.ts, docs/epics/per-repo-chat-turn-queue-outbox-E20261014613abdb3/HLD.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The three notices can be told apart from what createQueueFactory catches: a StoreUnavailable matching /newer plugin/, a node:sqlite load failure (ERR_UNKNOWN_BUILTIN_MODULE or a message naming node:sqlite), and any other failure.","evidence":"chat-queue-store.ts:342 throws StoreUnavailable('…made by a newer plugin…'), which matches /newer plugin/ as chat-queue-setup.ts:90 already tests. Lines 299-304 wrap an openDatabase failure as StoreUnavailable('the chat queue could not be opened: <original message>') without chaining the cause. The original error's `code` is therefore lost and the ERR_UNKNOWN_BUILTIN_MODULE check can never fire. The 'message naming node:sqlite' fallback still works, because Node's message ('No such built-in module: node:sqlite') is copied into the wrapped message. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-setup.ts]","action":"In the build, classify by the wrapped message (or chain `cause` in createChatQueueStore), and pin the test on a StoreUnavailable that wraps the sqlite error, not on a raw error.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every refusal from submitExternal is detectable and reported to the pane with its own note. A throw from outside the queue (opening the panel) is caught by handOver and becomes 'failed', and the recorded decision is kept.","evidence":"The worker returns refusals as { ok:false, reason, note } (chat-queue-store.ts:380, 411, 415-419), so the note can be carried into { kind:'unavailable', note }. The blank-text and no-CLI checks already run before the panel opens (chat-panel.ts:2244). docs-review-panel.ts:1603-1611: handOver catches any throw from notifyChat, logs it and returns 'failed'. The decision is recorded by the daemon before handOver is called (:1667). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-store.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac1, ac2 and ac3 each map to named tests in files and harnesses that exist: chat-queue-outbox-host.test.ts, docs-review-decision.test.ts and attachment-store.test.ts, plus the extension-chat-wiring harness for the disabled-chat wiring.","evidence":"Glob confirms that vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/ contains chat-queue-outbox-host.test.ts, docs-review-decision.test.ts, attachment-store.test.ts, extension-chat-wiring.test.ts, chat-queue-setup.test.ts and review-wiring.test.ts. §6's acceptance table maps ac1 to two tests, ac2 to two and ac3 to two. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-queue-outbox-host.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/attachment-store.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/extension-chat-wiring.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing tests that pin the old behaviour are named for rewriting, so the build will not leave stale assertions behind.","evidence":"chat-panel.test.ts:4999-5305 asserts 'sent' and 'queued' from the waiting list and a drop with a warning on dispose. review-wiring.test.ts:27 asserts the unconditional binding `notifyChat: (text) => chatHost.submitExternal(text),`. chat-queue-setup.ts:20-22 has the 'Messages run as before' notice that chat-queue-setup.test.ts pins. §6 and migration step 4 list all of them. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/review-wiring.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-queue-setup.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":15,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-14T18:37:11.922Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
